## Lore

The Nuhr (said "new hur") are Dwarves from a world much like Rifts Earth, with
both magic and technology, but technology closer to the eighteenth century and
its gunpowder. Their gift is a diluted Rune Magic, something like the Mystic
Kuznya of Russia, that enchants ordinary things by engraving them with runes;
almost every tool, weapon and device a Nuhr owns is enchanted, down to
rune-carved muskets.

Only a few thousand have reached Rifts Earth, nearly half of them in Queenston
Harbour. Most are craftsmen, weaponsmiths and builders who love the sea and
building boats, and about one in ten knows the rune craft. A notorious band of
them under Captain Sampson Rhees took up piracy on the Great Lakes, the Saint
Lawrence and the North Atlantic, raiding mainly the Coalition, Free Quebec, the
Minions of Splugorth, slavers and other pirates, and trading the plunder fairly
along the coast. That has made them folk heroes to many D-Bees and has branded
the whole race as pirates, to the annoyance of the law-abiding majority.

## GM Notes

Captain Sampson Rhees: a thickset Dwarf warrior of one hundred years,
Unprincipled 7th level Palladium Soldier, I.Q. 17, M.E. 11, M.A. 17, P.S. 22,
P.P. 10, P.E. 14, P.B. 8, Spd 10, 45 Hit Points, Nuhr Rune Mail (1D6x10+90
M.D.C.) and a Runic Axe (4D6 M.D.). In 104 P.A. he led 120-140 pirates; by
109 P.A. he leads nine ships with 467 Nuhr and 740 other D-Bee and human
pirates.

Size 4 feet to 4 feet 6 inches (1.2 to 1.4 m). Weight 120 to 200 pounds (54
to 90 kg). Life span 6D6+120 years, females about ten years longer; mature at
18. Also known as Pirate Dwarves and Mystic Dwarves.

Habitat: mostly Lazlo, Montreal and Free Quebec in eastern Canada, Michigan
and the northeastern United States; Nuhr pirates roam the Atlantic. Slave
market value 3D6x1,000 credits as warriors, sailors, pirates and labor, double
for skilled carpenters and builders, and 3D4x10,000 for Nuhr Rune Makers.
Allies: nothing formal, but most get on with humans and other civilized
people. Enemies: the Coalition States (especially its Navy), Free Quebec, the
Minions of Splugorth, the Horune, Bayou Ursines and other pirates; the Horune
are the Rhees Pirates'' great rivals.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nuhr-dwarf');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nuhr-dwarf';

